blished": "2026-05-27T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}, {"title": "13th Congressional District sees addition of Stockton, Trump-backed candidate", "source": "KMPH Fox 26", "published": "2026-05-22T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxNWFJtbGEtNk55UHdTYm14dlNXU3UxdmFuUzhFczFFbUdfeVhVYUw1cnAxcmlxSVk5OG11czVXTE80b2VvSFFPM3Y5d0dQQUd2eW1qR0hqM1puaEs1RG9FSGwzdGxrYk5pX1hsbkFEbGtLbGhMZWJCcUVuWXdzeS1BYnhETkhRQXJ6VUp6SjlUWU9tazAwZk1zT18xZmlWNUFHNkpQMm43cw?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 11.66, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": null, "poll_sd": null, "poll_weight": 0.0, "fundamentals": {"margin": 13.03, "lean": 2.0, "environment": 8.7, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.33}, "rating_margin": 10.75, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.13, "baseline_margin": 11.66, "analyst_adjustment": -1.16, "key_factors": ["Redistricting added Democratic-leaning Stockton, a major improvement on Gray's 187-vote 2024 margin in the old lines", "Gray holds a wide money edge ($1.2M to $450K cash) despite heavy Republican outside interest", "Expert ratings cluster at Likely D with several Safe/Solid D calls, and markets price Gray in the mid-90s", "No public general-election polling, and GOP leaders are investing heavily, signaling residual competitiveness"], "rationale": "Fundamentals, expert ratings, and prediction markets all point the same way: the redrawn district's Democratic lean, Gray's incumbency and fundraising edge, and a favorable national environment give him a clear advantage. His razor-thin 2024 win, Lincoln's Stockton roots, and millions in Republican investment keep this short of Safe.", "watch": "A late surge of Republican outside spending or the first public polls showing Lincoln competitive in Stockton would warrant moving this toward the tossup range.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Adam Gray (D) is running."]}, "overvie